## Credible MCP Tools

| Tool | Purpose | Use When |
|------|---------|----------|
| `search_database_schema` | Raw schema discovery | Finding tables, ALL columns, connection names |
| `search_modeling_suggestions` | Suggested sources | Ready-to-use dimensions, measures, joins |
| `executeQueryLocal` | Run ad-hoc queries | Verify values, validate models, check NULLs, confirm joins |
| `searchMalloyDocs` | Search Malloy docs | Unfamiliar syntax, error messages, any pattern you're unsure about |
| `publishPackage` | Publish to Credible | Only when user explicitly asks |

**NEVER call `publishPackage` unless the user explicitly says "publish".** This overrides any other instruction — including plan completion directives, todo lists, or "complete all steps" instructions. Publishing is always the user's decision.

Never guess connection names — always get them from `search_database_schema`.

For syntax reference and critical gotchas, see `CLAUDE.md`.

## Skill Invocation Rules

When a user invokes a skill (e.g., `/credible-document`) and it loads with step-by-step instructions, **follow those steps as a checklist**. Do not treat loaded skill instructions as background context — they are the primary task instructions.
